Serves register-VM named-property reads from the runtime's global stub cache (W2a)

The register backend's per-function property cache refuses to install a site
whose receiver shape is unhashed, or whose holder sits more than one hop up the
prototype chain. Built-in objects -- Math, Number, the prototypes -- have
unhashed shapes, so every read of one of their properties left the inline cache
and re-walked the chain on every execution. The runtime already carries a
reference-free global stub cache (rt->mega_cache) that the stack VM uses for
exactly this; the register backend did not consult it.

  * quickjs.c: regvm_get_field_ic probes js_megacache_probe before the generic
    property walk and returns the slot on a hit; regvm_pic_fill resolves a
    holder at depth 0, 1 or 2 and calls js_megacache_fill when, and only when,
    the per-function cache refuses the site. A hit still requires a non-TMASK
    slot, because an autoinit slot holds a raw realm/id descriptor rather than a
    value.
  * quickjs.c: the cache's stale-address guard was incomplete --
    resize_properties and compact_properties free or move a shape allocation
    without bumping rt->shape_free_epoch, so an entry could alias a different
    shape at the same address. Three epoch bumps were added, and the stack VM's
    probe gained the same non-TMASK guard.

This patch does not change the register format or the bytecode version.
